WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.400
The Walking Dead's tenth season finale&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:05.600
puts the spotlight on one of the&nbsp;
show's most notorious villains:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:10.240
Negan, and it's full of surprises. Here's&nbsp;
how the episode plays out, and what it means.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:15.840
The episode begins as Negan is exiled from the&nbsp;
community he helped save. He's given a cozy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:20.880
little house outside of town, and asked to not&nbsp;
return. While dealing with this unexpected exile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:25.440
Negan has a vision of himself in the past,&nbsp;
as the Negan we meet at the end of season 6.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:29.440
The presence of this previous version of&nbsp;
himself implies that, while he's clearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:33.840
changed a bit since he was defeated and locked&nbsp;
away, parts of his old self are still there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.800
Past-Negan chides present-day-Negan for trying&nbsp;
to win over the Alexandrians by playing nice.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:45.600
"It's time to face the facts, old&nbsp;
man. You are nothing without her."

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:51.280
The "her" here refers to Lucille, Negan's&nbsp;
trusty baseball bat. But, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:55.440
it also refers to Lucille, Negan's&nbsp;
wife, and the namesake of the bat.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:58.800
Negan appears disturbed by&nbsp;
the vision, but the next day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.560
he goes to the tree where he believes&nbsp;
his bat was buried after his showdown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:07.520
with Rick in season 8. This is when we get our&nbsp;
first flashback, to twelve years in the past.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:12.000
Negan is tied to a chair and a gang leader&nbsp;
called Baxter is interrogating him about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.200
where he found his supply of chemo drugs, which&nbsp;
is somewhat of a rarity in the post-apocalypse.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.600
It's clear that this Negan isn't the one we've&nbsp;
come to know later on. He's less self-assured,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.600
has a hard time killing walkers, and doesn't&nbsp;
quite have that swagger that has come to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:29.920
define his character. Negan begins to tell&nbsp;
the story of how he got the chemo drugs.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:35.440
The drugs Negan is carrying came from a mobile&nbsp;
medical clinic. In a flashback, he makes a feeble&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:40.000
attempt to rob the clinic's doctors, but someone&nbsp;
with a baseball bat quickly knocks him out.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.800
Eagle-eyed viewers will recognize his attacker as&nbsp;
Laura, who later becomes one of his most trusted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:49.520
allies in The Saviors. When Negan comes to,&nbsp;
he tells Franklin, the head of the operation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:53.520
the story of why he needs the drugs,&nbsp;
which begins flashback number three.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:56.640
Six weeks further into the past,&nbsp;
in the early days of the outbreak,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:00.960
Negan is living with his wife Lucille,&nbsp;
who's undergoing chemotherapy. Negan is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:04.880
an attentive and loving husband. However,&nbsp;
they're quickly running out of supplies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:09.520
and even though Lucille only has a few rounds&nbsp;
of chemo left, their remaining stash of drugs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:13.680
spoils during a fridge malfunction,&nbsp;
forcing him to rob the medical clinic.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:18.080
When Negan finishes telling his story,&nbsp;
they're remarkably generous and kind to him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:22.320
They feed him and give him the drugs he needs,&nbsp;
telling him they only want to help people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:25.040
Negan seems genuinely moved by their generosity.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:30.160
Thanks to these cascading flashbacks, fans&nbsp;
can finally see aspects of Negan's personality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:34.960
that were buried in the years that followed. He's&nbsp;
more vulnerable, without allies, real weapons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:38.400
or survival skills, and it changes&nbsp;
how he interacts with the world.

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:42.560
As Negan is leaving the clinic, Laura&nbsp;
gives him the familiar baseball bat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:46.480
they'd previously used to knock him&nbsp;
out. But there are even more flashbacks;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:51.360
in the midst of the scenes detailing Lucille's&nbsp;
chemo troubles, we're taken back to the earliest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:55.920
days of the outbreak. It also introduces a&nbsp;
different moment in Negan's personal growth.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.920
Pre-collapse Negan, as it turns out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:02.160
is a bit of a lout. He loses his job as a&nbsp;
gym teacher after beating someone up, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:07.120
he's spending his days playing video games. He's&nbsp;
also cheating on Lucille with one of her friends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:11.760
something that prevents him from being with her&nbsp;
when she first receives her cancer diagnosis.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:15.440
It's pretty clear how much Lucille's&nbsp;
cancer changed Negan — or, rather,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:19.520
how much his love for Lucille changed&nbsp;
him. Later, Negan weeps while Lucille&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:23.440
recounts how she learned about his affair,&nbsp;
but she tells him that she forgives him.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.040
"I want you to know that you made up for it."

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:33.600
The episode demonstrates just how transformative&nbsp;
those emotions were for him during the earliest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:37.680
days of the apocalypse, so how did he&nbsp;
then go on to become the Negan we know?

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:41.360
Back in the first flashback, Negan is&nbsp;
desperate to bring the chemo drugs he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:45.520
carrying back to Lucille, so he gives&nbsp;
up the location of the mobile clinic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:48.320
After the gang rounds up the&nbsp;
doctors, they let Negan go.

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:52.480
Lucille had previously begged Negan&nbsp;
to forget trying to save her life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:56.320
and instead just stay with her until she&nbsp;
died. When he finally arrives back at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.320 --> 00:04:00.000
home with the drugs, Negan discovers that&nbsp;
he should have listened to her. Lucille,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.080
now a walker, is on the bed in their room.&nbsp;
She appears to have purposefully overdosed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:08.640
on pills and tied one arm to the headboard&nbsp;
to prevent her from later attacking Negan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:12.640
Written on the door is a harrowing&nbsp;
phrase: "Please don't leave me like this."

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:18.000
It's a crushing moment for Negan, who's spent the&nbsp;
entire apocalypse trying to keep Lucille alive.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:21.760
After sitting with her for a while,&nbsp;
he goes outside to a nearby fence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:25.760
and uses some barbed wire to put the&nbsp;
final touches on Lucille the bat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:29.440
Once he's said goodbye to Lucille&nbsp;
the person, he burns down the house.

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:32.960
Back at the gang hideout, Franklin&nbsp;
is being tortured for information&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:36.240
about where he gets his medical&nbsp;
supplies from. Negan puts a stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:39.760
to it by killing most of the gang&nbsp;
members, but leaving Baxter alive.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:42.960
It's here where viewers get their&nbsp;
first glimpse of the Negan they know.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:46.960
Dressed in his signature leather&nbsp;
jacket and brandishing his bat Lucille,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:52.080
Negan tells Baxter about the man he beat up who&nbsp;
got him fired. But now, the rules have changed.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:58.000
"Now, when I see red, it's just a&nbsp;
question of what I am capable of."

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:04.560
Back in the present day, Negan digs up Lucille the&nbsp;
bat and brings it home to his cabin. He speaks to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:09.680
it as though it's Lucille herself, apologizing for&nbsp;
leaving her, and even apologizing for naming his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:15.520
baseball bat after her. Negan then places Lucille&nbsp;
the bat into his fireplace and watches it burn.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:20.080
But things aren't quite that cut and dry. The&nbsp;
next day, Negan strolls back into Alexandria.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:24.160
When Carol confronts him, he tells her that&nbsp;
he's not interested in living in exile.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:28.000
Carol says that Maggie will kill him if&nbsp;
he moves back, and makes it clear that now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:32.640
that she's tried to help Negan, she won't&nbsp;
intervene. Negan agrees and continues on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:37.600
looking at an infuriated Maggie as he walks by.&nbsp;
The mischievous grin he wears while he observes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:41.840
her suggests that Negan's new chapter&nbsp;
won't necessarily include peacemaking.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:46.960
Based on how season 10 ends, it feels inevitable&nbsp;
that the conflict between Maggie and Negan will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:51.840
boil over very soon — and that it won't be&nbsp;
pretty. While Negan's past reveals that he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:57.200
a complex character and that his propensity for&nbsp;
violence is just one facet of his personality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.200 --> 00:06:01.360
it also demonstrates that violence is&nbsp;
something that has always existed within him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:03.360
even if it's hidden under the surface.

